  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Studios and clients pay for clear drawings and good design thinking. They judge you by portfolio, accuracy and communication.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is measuring a space accurately and drawing it to scale.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and software and skill courses for architecture students: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools generate concepts and renderings. Routine presentation drafts shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Design judgment, site understanding and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explore and refine; later, own the design decision.
  </p>

